    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10366" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπλεονεκτέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>have equal precedence</i> or
				<i>privilege,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῷ οὐρανῷ τό τε μέσον αὐτοῦ
					καὶ τὸ πέριξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simp.
					<u>in Cael.</u>
					515.5
				</span></i>
			; <i>have respective advantages over each other,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				335.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Elias
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				98.1
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπήρ-ησις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				341.2
			</span></i>.</div>
